<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [924].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>924&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;PEAT MEDIUM 2 FOR METHANOBACTERIA</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Major metals (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=923">923</a>)                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace metal 2 solution (see below)                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, bring to a boil for 5 min, then, cool down under a stream of a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture.  Distribute the medium into Balch-type culture tubes (5 ml each) under the same gas mixture, seal with thick blue butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  <br>
To complete the medium, add the following solutions to each of culture tubes (containing 5 ml medium) from sterile anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 83 mM TiNTA solution* (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=923">923</a>)            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1.0 M MES solution* (pH 7.45)                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.10&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution* (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=923">923</a>)                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1% Yeast extract solution                              </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.01&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 50 mM Coenzyme M solution                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.025&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 10 mM Sodium acetate                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.015&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 4 mM Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution*                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Pressurize the tubes to 70 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) and allow to stand for at least 7 hr.  Check the final pH of the medium to be about 5.7.  <br>
<I>Trace metal 2 solution:</I> <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace metal solution 1 (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=923">923</a>)           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> EDTA&#183;2Na                                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;37.23&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Adjust pH to 7.0 with NaOH.       <br>
